   "Notes": "Raised 2026-08-22 with the research-question architecture (docs/phd/research-questions.md, data/research-questions.csv). Deliberately left open: the lead strand should be decided by which advisor engages first, not chosen in advance - that is what the architecture is for. All seven strands are answerable from the same fieldwork, so the choice changes the framing and the primary supervisor, not the field design. Resolve by marking exactly one RQ row Status=Lead once a supervisor conversation is live. Sequencing note: the P1 literature components (data/lit-components.csv) are shared across strands, so reading is not blocked on this. RE-AFFIRMED 2026-08-22: left open a second time, deliberately, on unchanged reasoning. Nothing in the OQ-16 or OQ-17 decisions of the same date bears on it - the coffee setting and the deferred novelty relocation are both compatible with all seven strands.",
