   "ID": "EXP-22",
   "Theme": "Data infrastructure",
   "Type": "Field RCT with costing",
   "Geography": "Adaptable - any originator running two protocols",
   "Population": "Loan officers and originating groups",
   "Community_Context": "An originator willing to run two origination protocols side by side",
   "Problem": "The claim that designing for securitisation at origination beats retrofitting it has never been tested, and neither has its cost. Everyone in the sector repeats it; nobody has priced it. Note that the estimand depends on WHAT THE CONTROL ARM ACTUALLY IS: against a professionalised MFI with a working MIS the treatment measures the marginal cost of extra fields, but LIT-031 shows cooperative internal credit funds are often informal and unregulated with weak accounting, and against that counterfactual the treatment measures the cost of building a protocol from near-zero. Different quantities; originator type is a pre-specified moderator, not a nuisance.",
   "SDG_Refs": "SDG 1; SDG 8",
   "Product_Concept": "Securitisation-ready origination protocol (full RT-1 field set) versus the originator's standard protocol, on randomly assigned branches or officers.",
   "Design": "Cluster-randomised protocol assignment (branch level where cluster count allows, otherwise officer level within branch, accepting contamination that biases toward the null) with activity-based costing of both arms. Cluster COUNT is the binding constraint, not household sample size - a mid-size originator has 10-40 branches. Stratify on branch size and maturity; multi-originator recruitment is the fallback. Treatment uses the full RT-1 field set through the originator's EXISTING capture tool, extended - never a new app, which would confound protocol cost with tool-adoption cost. Fallback ladder: branch randomisation, officer randomisation, stepped wedge, then unrandomised time-and-motion, which is a costing exercise and not an experiment.",
   "Primary_Outcome": "ONE primary: marginal operational cost per household originated, treatment minus control, by activity-based costing on timestamped capture logs (self-reported time is systematically biased and is a validity check only). Secondary families: cost structure (the H2 learning curve against cumulative originations; the H3 per-field cost distribution, which yields a ranked cost curve an originator can adopt incrementally), record quality, officer and borrower burden, and - DEFERRED, not gating - default predictability once the cohort seasons. The tracker row previously named cost and predictability as co-primaries; they run on incompatible clocks, so predictability is pre-registered and postponed, and RQ-21 is reallocated to EXP-25's retrospective panels, which already contain seasoned defaults.",
   "Toolbox_Fit": "The direct test of RQ-06 and one of the two falsification tests that can run before any product pilot. Turns RT-1 from a design document into a costed proposition, and its validator doubles as a live test of the schema - a field the validator keeps rejecting is a schema defect, not an officer error. Spec at docs/research/experiments/exp-22-origination-protocol-costing.md.",
   "RQ_Refs": "RQ-01; RQ-06; RQ-21; RQ-22",
   "Candidate_Partners": "An MFI or savings-group network with branch-level operations, or a cooperative union with an internal credit fund (different estimand - see Problem). Screen for CLUSTER COUNT before enthusiasm. Requires HR or staff-representation approval for officer time measurement, which is a separate approval from the data-sharing agreement and is the one that gets forgotten.",
   "Candidate_Funders": "FSD Africa; IDRC",
