   "Community_Context": "Historical management-information-system data from one or more originators across regions",
   "Problem": "The pooling thesis rests on defaults being idiosyncratic rather than covariate. They are covariate - but through TWO separable channels, and only one of them is diversifiable. The environmental channel (weather, pathogen, price) is agro-climatic and can in principle be diversified across regions. The institutional channel (market saturation, multiple borrowing, contagion) is a MARKET-level factor: LIT-037 finds individual lender growth does not predict portfolio deterioration while market-level penetration does. If that is the operative factor, a pool assembled from several lenders in one country is not diversified against the thing that historically predicts trouble.",
   "SDG_Refs": "SDG 17",
   "Product_Concept": "No product. Estimate default correlation across groups, regions, time and agro-climatic zones from existing portfolio data.",
   "Design": "Retrospective multi-level variance-components study on administrative loan panels. Hierarchical GLMM (discrete-time survival form where censoring is recorded) over borrower / group / branch / agro-climatic zone / lender / market, with lender CROSSED against zone - that crossing is what separates the institutional channel from the environmental one, and it is why the design needs at least two lenders per market and at least two markets. Plus an explicit mapping step: fit a single-factor Vasicek model to recover the asset correlation the tools actually consume.",
   "Primary_Outcome": "The MARKET-level intra-class correlation of loan default, with its confidence interval. Secondary: the full ICC decomposition by level; the penetration interaction (LIT-037 thresholds tested on loan-level data for the first time); cross-market portability of each component (RQ-28); and the recovered asset correlation rho fed to RT-5.",
   "Toolbox_Fit": "Feeds RT-5 the one parameter its own documentation calls the one that matters most, and which it currently handles with a sweep from independence to near-perfect correlation. Also supplies the asset correlation that LIT-038 shows the Pluto-Tasche PD bound takes as an ASSUMED input - so this experiment converts an assumption into an estimate. A falsification test that can run before any pilot exists. Spec at docs/research/experiments/exp-25-default-correlation.md.",
   "RQ_Refs": "RQ-03; RQ-13; RQ-28",
